          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            there is an
            %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/cohesive%20(infinity,1)-topos#ChernWeilTheory"} intrinsic notion of ∞-Chern-Weil theory
            that gives rise to a notion of
            %em connection
            on
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+group"} ∞-Lie group
            %em connection
            on a smooth
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            is a structure that supports the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+homomorphism+in+Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Chern-Weil homomorphism in Smooth∞Grpd
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi smooth
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in H^1_{smooth}(X,G)
            of the bundle and the refinements to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            of its
            = succeed "es:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+characteristic+form"} curvature characteristic class
          %p
            This generalizes the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
            and the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+homomorphism"} Chern-Weil homomorphism
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
          %p
            See the
            %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory+in+Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd#Motivation"} Motivation section
            at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory+in+Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Chern-Weil theory in Smooth∞Grpd
            and the page
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+theory+introduction"} ∞-Chern-Weil theory introduction
            for more background.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#for_braided_groups
            For braided
            = succeed "-groups" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            equippd with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔾
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Grp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G} \in Grp(\mathbf{H})
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+%E2%88%9E-group"} braided ∞-group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi curv
                    %mi 𝔾
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi 𝔾
